From: vyos-ls1046a-build CI <ci@local>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dpaa/fman: raise CC-tree static key cap 32 -> 64

T-M6-8 VLAN throughput investigation, board evidence (2026-08-31).

FMAN_CC_MAX_STATIC_KEYS/FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_MAX_KEYS were both set to 32,
chosen as a conservative MURAM budget (~5 KiB) rather than any hardware
limit -- the CC-tree hardware supports up to 255 keys/node. That
software cap turned out to sit exactly on the edge of a routine
workload: an 8-stream bidirectional iperf3 test (`-P 8 --bidir`) opens
16 separate TCP connections (8 forward + 8 reverse), and nf_flowtable
offloads both the orig and reply tuple per connection, needing 32
concurrent CC keys on one port for a clean run. With zero headroom,
any transient overlap during stream setup/teardown (an old flow not yet
torn down while a new one arrives) pushes a fresh install over the cap,
observed on the board as ~91% of REPLACE attempts failing with
fe_flow_insert=-28 (-ENOSPC) and the bulk of that test's traffic falling
back to kernel software forwarding (matching the CPU softirq jumping
from ~0% idle to ~50% the instant traffic starts).

Raise both caps to 64, giving 2x headroom over that measured minimum.
64 keys x ~150 B is ~10 KiB of the 64 KiB MURAM budget -- comfortable
headroom even with multiple ports concurrently using VLAN CC-tree
offload. FMAN_CC_MAX_STATIC_KEYS (dpaa_fman_caps.h, consumed by
ask_vlan_cc.c's per-port key array and rebuild-tree allocation) and
FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_MAX_KEYS (fman_pcd.h, the silicon-programming layer's
own bound in fman_pcd_cc_static_install()) are two independently
defined constants kept in sync by review (per the existing comment on
the latter) -- both must move together or fman_pcd_cc_static_install()
would reject any tree above the old 32-key silicon-side cap regardless
of the software-side array growing.

Companion change (separate commit, OOT ask.ko mirror header): the
ask_fman_caps.h copy of FMAN_CC_MAX_STATIC_KEYS is bumped identically.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate | Risk-Tier: B (widens an existing bound, no new API)
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_fman_caps.h b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_fman_caps.h
index 9144232fc..3a1c8e8f1 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_fman_caps.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_fman_caps.h
@@ -190,9 +190,10 @@
  * Passed to fman_cc_tree_install() for the static (default/vpp) lifecycle.
  * The dynamic (ask) lifecycle builds the same key one-at-a-time via
  * fman_cc_tree_add_key(). FMAN_CC_MAX_STATIC_KEYS bounds the static tree
- * at the ~5 KiB MURAM budget from spec sec 3.5 (32 keys x ~150 B).
+ * at the ~10 KiB MURAM budget from spec sec 3.5 (64 keys x ~150 B; raised
+ * from 32 2026-08-31, T-M6-8 VLAN throughput investigation).
  */
-#define FMAN_CC_MAX_STATIC_KEYS	32
+#define FMAN_CC_MAX_STATIC_KEYS	64

 struct fman_cc_static_tree {
 	u16 num_keys;
diff --git a/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h b/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
index 68f8a1ac85d8..1a2b3c4d5e6f 100644
--- a/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
+++ b/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
@@ -272,9 +272,10 @@
  */

 /* Bounds mirror FMAN_CC_MAX_STATIC_KEYS in dpaa_fman_caps.h (kept in sync
- * by review; the install body re-checks num_keys against this).
+ * by review; the install body re-checks num_keys against this). Raised
+ * 32 -> 64 2026-08-31, T-M6-8 VLAN throughput investigation.
  */
-#define FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_MAX_KEYS	32
+#define FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_MAX_KEYS	64

 /* Match-key field-presence bitmask for struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_key.present. */
 #define FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_ETHERTYPE	BIT(0)
